                <pb facs="0288" n="238" sameAs="frus:frus1918Russiav03/pg238"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 861.77/445</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Consul at
                        Vladivostok</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Caldwell</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1918-08-15"><hi rendition="#italic">August 15,
                        1918</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>The American railway contingent which arrived Vladivostok August 11 was ordered
                    there with the view of assisting in the reorganization and operation of the
                    Siberian Railway. It is hoped that it will receive the support and cooperation
                    of all political parties and governmental factions. After communicating to
                    officials this telegram should be made public.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Lansing</hi></signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
